  {
   "heading": "Overview / Tổng quan",
   "segment_index": "S2.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survey_analysis.qmd:29-30",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survey_analysis.vn.qmd:16-16",
   "proposition": "The English says that some of the chapter's survey-package-based CODE derives from early versions of the EPIET case studies; the Vietnamese says that the survey PACKAGE itself derives from early versions of the EPIET case studies (\"Một số package **survey** dựa trên các phiên bản đầu tiên của các nghiên cứuu trường hợp EPIET\").",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader is told the CRAN survey package was built from EPIET teaching case studies, which is false, and loses the actual attribution that the example code shown in this chapter was adapted from those case studies.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Sampling bias / Sai số chọn mẫu",
   "segment_index": "S14.P1",
   "kind": "missing",
   "en_span": "chapters/survey_analysis.qmd:591-593",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survey_analysis.vn.qmd:467-467",
   "proposition": "The English states that the descriptive discussion or age-pyramid visualisation of the sample-versus-source distributions is MORE IMPORTANT THAN the binomial test itself; the Vietnamese states only that the descriptive discussion \"is important\" (\"là quan trọng\") and drops the comparison with the binomial test.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader keeps treating the binomial p-values as the primary evidence for sampling bias, instead of demoting them below the descriptive comparison, which is exactly the priority the paragraph exists to set.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
